#
# The Rust notices and the licence texts under them are digest-bound: their
# SHA-256 is recorded in tools/notices/*.tsv and rechecked on every platform.
#
# Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf enabled by default, which would
# rewrite every line ending and change every digest, so these paths are kept
# byte for byte as committed.
#
# They also quote upstream licence texts verbatim, and some of those carry
# trailing whitespace. Reformatting them would be editing someone else's
# licence, so the whitespace checks are off for these paths rather than the
# text being cleaned up.
licences/rust/*.md      -text -whitespace
tools/notices/texts/*   -text -whitespace
tools/notices/*.tsv     -text
